# Manual-defined oracle differences for sst68030_solo. See tests/SstKnown.h.

# D23a (redefined 2026-11-26): an enabled 6888x exception on FMOVE FPn,<ea>
# is a mid-instruction one, taken after the store (MC68881UM-1989 § 6.1):
# format $9, 20 bytes (MC68030UM-1989 Figure 10-43), where the oracle stacks
# format $3, 12 bytes. Each tagged vector's expected state is derived from
# the oracle's (tests/SstKnown.h): the manual's frame 8 bytes lower, A7 and
# whatever the handler stacked below it with it, the internal register not
# compared. Everything else is compared as recorded; a vector that then
# agrees counts as agreement, and a stale oracle frame fails the gate.
@D23a 0017f4 | fpu/identity seed=711 #370
@D23a 0017f0 | fpu/off seed=710 #391
@D23a 0017f4 | fpu/tt seed=712 #394

# D12: manual-defined group-2 instruction address; all other state stays compared.
